{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to the given base, returning its string representation. Raises ValueError if the base is not valid (i.e., base <= 1 or base >= 10).\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (1 < base < 10):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid base: base must be greater than 1 and less than 10.\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    return \"\".join(result[::-1])"}
